## §7. Validation

### §7.1 Per-commit gates

| Commit | Validation |
|---|---|
| 1 (D1) | New tests green; manual: run `pytest -k "extract_proposal_index"`; smoke: feed real anonymized 78KB aggregator output to a unit-tested helper, assert `proposals.json` appears |
| 2 (D2) | New tests green; manual: feed the real LLM constraint dict `{"type":"ordering","rule":"..."}`; assert it parses; assert `ProposalIndex.from_dict()` with 1 valid + 1 malformed constraint keeps 1 |
| 3 (D3 primitives) | `test_protocols.py` + `test_parsers.py` green; lint clean |
| 4 (D3 handler) | Handler tests green; `default_registry()` count test green; pytest of `conversational/` package green |
| 5 (D3 UI) | `npm test` in `react-shared` green; snapshot for widget matches; Storybook story renders if configured |
| 6 (SOP fixes) | `test_all_sops_lint_clean.py` green; manual: run SOP linter on `model_optimization/SOP.md`; confirm `proposal_selection` resolves in `tool_to_phase_map`; smoke: run SOP runtime with stub LLM returning canned proposals → confirm Phase 3b widget appears and selection propagates to Phase 4 |
| 7 (RankEvolve) | RankEvolve full test suite green; manual smoke: launch rankevolve session, complete proposal selection, confirm overrides API still wired |

### §7.2 End-to-end smoke (after Commits 1–6 in AF)

```bash
# NOTE — the SOP CLI lives at agent_foundation.resources.tools.sop
# (verified: src/agent_foundation/resources/tools/sop/__main__.py and cli.py).
# An earlier draft of this plan used "agent_foundation.cli.sop_tool" which
# does not exist; the correct module path is below.

# 1. Trigger research-propose end-to-end
python -m agent_foundation.resources.tools.sop model_optimization \
    "<your research goal>" \
    --until "Phase 3"
# → produces <ws>/outputs/proposals.json (D1+D2 prove themselves here)
# → phase_outputs["proposals_path"] populated by Commit 1b

# 2. Pause at Phase 3b (proposal_selection widget)
python -m agent_foundation.resources.tools.sop --resume <session-id> \
    --until "Phase 3b"
# → handler resolves proposals via the I4 priority chain (Commit 4):
#     tool_args["proposals_path"]
#       OR phase_outputs["proposals_path"]  ← this is the AF default path
#       OR rankevolve back-compat keys
# → widget renders with the 40 proposals; user selects "P1,P3"

# 3. Run Phase 4 (consumes the selection)
python -m agent_foundation.resources.tools.sop --resume <session-id> \
    --until "Phase 4"
# → SOP body reads phase_outputs[Phase 3][proposals_path]
#                   phase_outputs[Phase 3b][selected_proposal_ids]
# → task --use-proposal <ws>/outputs/proposals.json --proposal-ids P1,P3
# → _proposal_plan.md inlines P1 + P3
# → _picked_proposals.json audit written

# Acceptance:
#   <ws>/outputs/proposals.json exists                              (D1+D2)
#   phase_outputs[Phase 3][proposals_path] == <ws>/outputs/...      (D1b)
#   phase_outputs[Phase 3b][selected_proposal_ids] == ["P1","P3"]   (D3)
#   task workspace contains _picked_proposals.json                  (F4)
#   task plan inlines only P1 and P3 (not all 40)                   (F4 integration)
```

**Yolo-mode equivalent** (single command, no `--resume`):
```bash
python -m agent_foundation.resources.tools.sop model_optimization \
    "<your research goal>" --yolo
```
Yolo mode auto-applies the `tool.json` `yolo_default` for `proposal_selection` (`mode: select_all`) so the smoke test runs end-to-end without manual selection — useful for CI.

### §7.3 Regression net (permanent)

- `test_all_sops_lint_clean.py` — defends every SOP author from now on.
- `test_conversation_tool_registry_size` — asserts exactly 6 handlers (intentional code edit required to change).
- `test_proposal_constraint_aliases` — locks in the `type→kind` / `rule→reason` aliases so they don't silently regress.
- `test_bta_file_fallback` — locks in the truncated-response file-fallback path.

